        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points through card combinations (fifteens, pairs, runs, flushes) and be first to reach the target score (typically 31 or 61).',
          gameplay: '1. Four cards dealt to each player. 2. Non-dealer cuts for starter card (turn-up). 3. Players alternately play cards to the pile, pegging points for fifteens, pairs, runs during play. 4. After all cards played, hands are counted for combinations. 5. Starter card applies to both hands.',
          keyRules: [
            'Four cards dealt (no crib)',
            'Ace always counts 1 (never 11)',
            "Starter card (turn-up) counts for both players' hands",
            'Play to 31 without exceeding during pegging',
            'Similar pegging and counting to Cribbage but simpler',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Similar to Cribbage strategy: try to make fifteens and pairs during play. Keep cards that work well together for the counting phase.',
          intermediate: "Since there's no crib, focus entirely on your own hand strength. The starter card is crucialâ€”hands can change dramatically based on what turns up.",
          advanced: "Card counting during play to predict opponent's holdings. Optimizing play order to maximize pegging opportunities while minimizing opponent's chances.",
          tips: [
            'Without a crib, you can play more aggressively in your hand construction',
            "Ace is always 1â€”no 'one for his nob' equivalent for Ace",
